In a recent posting, I asked for suggestions for how to get from the right
side of the castle level anywhere-anywhere, that is, other than one level
deeper.  A bunch of people e-mailed responses; I've collected what they said
below, with my responses:


1)  Kill something, let it rot, eat it (which will, with luck, confuse me)
and zap the wond of teleport at myself.  But not on the castle level.

Unfortunately, every time I ate something, either I was no longer confused
by the time I finished or I felt deathly sick.

2)  Dig through the top of the castle.

Tried this.  Prob'ly dug in the wrong place-it didn't work.  Anyone who 
knows exactly where to dig, where is it?

3)  Jump over the trapdoors.

No jumping boots.

4)  Fill the trapdoors with boulders.

Not enough boulders.

4a)  Get stone giants in there--they have boulders.

I'm not that lucky.

5)  Freeeze the moat with a wand of cold.

No wand of cold, nothing to polymorph with other than a chamelion corpse.

6)  Boil it with a wand of fire. (?)

Tried this repeatedly.  No apparent change.  Maybe if I tried a few more 
times, but . . . I did have a wand of fire (about 4) and knew fireball (the
spell).  Once again, no luck.

7)  Get confused by an umber hulk, then teleport.

Umber hulks need to be at least one square away to confuse you, and they
need to be lit.  Or so it seems, for I tried this one also.  Had three U's
wandering around on level 30 for a while, then mercy-killed them.

8)  Use the wand of teleport.

But teleport doesn't work on the castle level, and it is useless to waste it
on the hell level.

9)  There's a pretty good chance you'll find a level teleporter in the maze
below the castle.

No such luck.  A magic trap and a poly trap, but no level teleport.

10)  You could also get lucky and find a potion of confusion or a potion of
booze.

No luck so far...

11)  Maybe there's a ring of levitation in the maze.

Not unless a monster is carrying it when I kill it.

12)  Mud boots are *USUALLY* water-walking boots.  Maybe if you kill enough
monsters in the sub-castle level one of them will leave you a pair in its
will.  Or maybe boots of levitation.

Maybe, but it has yet to happen.

13)  It seems that your character is strong enough that you don't need a WoW:
Why make the game any easier for yourself????  Skip the castle, and go 
plunder vlad's castle, get the amulet, and hopefully by that time you've
gotten a ring of levitation.

Because I need to level teleport down to Vlad and the Wiz, but I don't have 
the requisite equiptment.

Thanks to those who replied, and another request for suggestions from all.

